s of Axis shipping between 1941 and 1942. The base was a priority target for Axis aerial attacks and was heavily bombed in 1942, which forced a withdrawal of the flotilla from Malta to Alexandria, where the ships of the Mediterranean Fleet had already moved.","LocalizedString":"HMS Talbot, also known as the 10th Submarine Flotilla, was the name of the Royal Navy's submarine base at Manoel Island, Malta, from 1941 to 1943. The base hosted submarines from both the Royal Navy and the Polish Navy, and the flotilla never counted more than 12 submarines at the time. Despite its small size, it managed to sink 412,575 tons of Axis shipping between 1941 and 1942. The base was a priority target for Axis aerial attacks and was heavily bombed in 1942, which forced a withdrawal of the flotilla from Malta to Alexandria, where the ships of the Mediterranean Fleet had already moved."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::CurrentExpansion","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardReceiveDamage"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Class_Specific/War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2.0"},"soundAttack":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'AU_Order_UBoat_04'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Orders/U_Boat/AU_Order_UBoat_04.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/CandidateArtwork/Summer_24/t_hms_talbot.t_hms_talbot","SubPathString":""},"artist":"British WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/HMS_TALBOT.HMS_TALBOT","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":339.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_hms_talbot_photo","SourceString":"HMS Una leaving HMS Talbot for a patrol, date unknown.","LocalizedString":"HMS Una leaving HMS Talbot for a patrol, date unknown."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game